  "body": "First slice of the hole cycles: the **ream** (feed in, feed out, no dwell) as a cycle choice on the existing drilling operation.\n\n## What changed\n- `CycleKind::Ream` (cl) / `CycleChoice::Ream` (motion): the chain plunges to the bottom at the plunge feed and feeds back to R at the same feed (G85 posts one F word for both moves), dwell dropped. Rides the bore door: the tool must fit the hole, a stepped hole is refused, no centre-cutting requirement. Never chosen by Auto. Radial (cross) reaming refused by name.\n- Stream word `CYCLE REAM`; project spelling `\"ream\"` (params and cached cycle); setup sheet name.\n- Posts: fanuc, haas, mazak, doosan-dnm, sinumerik, tormach, grblhal and fanuc-lathe map REAM to G85. Each canned map now ends with an `else` that refuses an unknown cycle word by name instead of falling through to another cycle. Heidenhain joins its explicit-chain branch (feed out). TinyG/Carvera expand as before; sinker/wire/plasma posts refuse.\n- UI: drill page Cycle combo gains \"Ream (feed in, feed out)\"; index mapping moved to `operations::cycle_from_index` beside `cycle_index`.\n- MCP: `edit_operation` takes `{\"cycle\":\"ream\"}` through the same undoable `EditOperationParams`; unknown words refused.\n- `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` (REAM), `docs/decisions/1445-hole-cycles.md`.\n\n## Sources\nRS-274/NGC canned cycles (NIST IR 6556, The NIST RS274NGC Interpreter v3) and LinuxCNC's G-code reference for G85's shape. No vendor post, manual text or CAM output read.\n\n## Tests\n- motion `drilling::tests_ream`: `ream_feeds_in_and_out_at_the_plunge_feed_without_dwell`, `ream_is_never_the_auto_answer`, `ream_refuses_a_tool_that_will_not_enter_and_a_stepped_hole`, `ream_reads_the_hole_as_pre_drilled`; `tests_cross` loop includes Ream.\n- post `tests/ream_cycle.rs`: `the_stream_names_the_ream_and_reads_back`, `canned_posts_write_g85_and_no_other_cycle`, `expanding_posts_feed_out_of_the_reamed_hole`, `posts_without_drilling_refuse_a_ream`, `the_named_posts_post_the_ream_byte_exact` (new goldens `tests/golden/ream/{fanuc,haas,heidenhain,sinumerik,grblhal,tormach}.nc`).\n- app `tests/ream_cycle.rs`: `ream_is_an_undoable_drill_parameter_that_generates_feed_out_and_round_trips`, `a_ream_with_a_tool_wider_than_the_hole_is_refused_by_name`, `mcp_edit_operation_sets_and_refuses_the_cycle_by_its_project_spelling`.\n- ui `egui_app::tests::cycle_combo`: `every_cycle_has_one_label_and_picks_itself_back`, `the_ream_reads_in_plain_english_and_an_unknown_index_is_auto`.\n- Gate: quick falls back to batch (cl touched); ran targeted instead: all cl + post suites (every existing golden byte-identical), motion lib + center_cut/cross suites, app lib + 23 drilling/project/post/MCP/golden suites, ui lib (676 pass), clippy `-D warnings` on cl/post/motion/app/ui. No existing golden or snapshot changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The posted output was **not run on a real control**; the goldens are our mapping's regression records.\n- The ream on lathe posts (fanuc-lathe G85, tormach-lathe) is not pinned (#1481).\n- The unknown-cycle `else` refusal in the posts is defence in depth: the stream parser already rejects unknown kinds, so no test reaches it.\n- Full batch tier not run (targeted suites above); GUI not launched.\n\n## Follow-ups\n- #1479 fine boring with user-given orientation and shift (not guessed)\n- #1480 boring with dwell and feed out (G89 P), dwell units per post\n- #1481 ream on the lathe posts\n\nChangelog: Drilling: a Ream cycle (feed in, feed out) posts as G85 on canned-cycle posts and as an explicit feed-out chain elsewhere (#1445)\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #1445\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
